  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have a tree with NNN vertices rooted at vertex 111.\n\nColor each vertex of the tree either red or blue such that the expression\n\n∣cR−cB∣+∣sR−sB∣|c_R - c_B| + |s_R - s_B|∣cR​−cB​∣+∣sR​−sB​∣is minimized, where:\n\n\ncRc_RcR​ is the number of vertices colored red, and cBc_BcB​ is the number of vertices colored blue.\nsRs_RsR​ is the score of the color red, and sBs_BsB​ is the score of the color blue. These can be computed as follows:\n\nConsider some vertex uuu (1≤u≤N1 \\leq u \\leq N1≤u≤N), and look at the subtree†^\\dagger† of uuu.\nIf there are strictly more red vertices than blue vertices in this subtree, add 111 to the score of red.\nOtherwise, if the number of red vertices and blue vertices in the subtree of uuu are equal, and uuu is colored red, add 111 to the score of red.\nOtherwise, add 111 to the score of blue.\n\n\nFind any coloring of the tree that **minimizes** the above expression.\n\n†^\\dagger† Vertex vvv is said to lie in the subtree of vertex uuu, if the unique simple path from 111 to vvv in the tree contains uuu.\n\nIn particular, uuu lies within its own subtree.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of vertices\nin the tree.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a string of length NNN containing only the characters `R` and `B`, where the iii-th of these characters denotes the color of the iii-th node of the tree.\n\n\nIf there are multiple possible colorings that minimize ∣cR−cB∣+∣sR−sB∣|c_R - c_B| + |s_R - s_B|∣cR​−cB​∣+∣sR​−sB​∣, you may print any of them.\n\n\nNote that the output **is case-sensitive**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The input edges describe a tree on NNN vertices",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
